  "description": "AWITUX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H60 N12 O20 Tb4,4(C1 H4 O1),5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.841-3.961 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 107.21-115.49°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tb4(LH2)4(μ2-OH)4]·4CH3OH·5H2O (C64H60N12O20Tb4·4CH4O·5H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
